{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, sorry you're having trouble. I'd like to help, but I need a bit more detail first. Could you tell me: (1) What isn't working? For example email, Teams, VPN, your Mac, a printer, or a particular app. (2) What happens when you try? Please include any error message, word for word, or a screenshot. (3) When did it start, and does it happen every time? Your account looks fine and your laptop is online, so the problem doesn't seem to be a lockout or a password issue. One thing I did spot: your mailbox is about 99% full. Once it hits 100%, you can't send email anymore and Outlook may stop syncing. If your problem is with email, that's probably the cause. You can free up space by emptying Deleted Items and Junk Email, and by sorting your Inbox and Sent Items by size so you can delete large attachments or save them to OneDrive. Reply with the details above and I'll take it from there.",
  "internal_note": "The ticket is vague (\"it's not working\"), so I'm asking the user for details. What I checked: lookup_user shows the account is active, with 0 failed logins, not blocked, VPN enabled, and no forced password change. The mailbox is at 99.4% (50890/51200 MB), which is the most likely cause if this is an email problem (KB-010), but I haven't confirmed that. Laptop BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15) is online, checked in recently, has 14.6% disk free, and shows no warnings. Sign-in logs for the last 14 days show all successful logins from Chicago with Duo push and nothing unusual. I haven't taken or queued any action. Once the user replies: if it's email, follow the KB-010 cleanup steps, and escalate for a quota increase (with manager approval) if the mailbox is still over 95% afterwards.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-010"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
